{"name":"Hanover","hex":"#dac5b1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hanover","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["British family that ruled from 1714 to 1901, more commonly known as the Georgian, Regency and Victorian periods.","The capital city of Lower Saxony, Germany."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hanover"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hanover","blocks":[{"text":"Hanover is the capital and largest city of the German state of Lower Saxony. Its population of 535,932 (2021) makes it the 13th-largest city in Germany as well as the fourth-largest in northern Germany after Berlin, Hamburg and Bremen. Hanover's urban area comprises the towns of Garbsen, Langenhagen and Laatzen and has a population of about 791,000 (2018). The Hanover Region has some 1.16 million inhabitants (2019) and is the largest in the Hanover–Braunschweig–Göttingen–Wolfsburg Metropolitan Region, the 17th biggest metropolitan area by GDP in the European Union."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Hannover_Blick_Neues_Rathaus_01.jpg/330px-Hannover_Blick_Neues_Rathaus_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanover","wikidata":"Q1715"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Hannover_old_townhall_Karmarschstrasse_Mitte_Hannover_Germany_01.jpg/500px-Hannover_old_townhall_Karmarschstrasse_Mitte_Hannover_Germany_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Hannover_old_townhall_Karmarschstrasse_Mitte_Hannover_Germany_01.jpg/1280px-Hannover_old_townhall_Karmarschstrasse_Mitte_Hannover_Germany_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Hannover_old_townhall_Karmarschstrasse_Mitte_Hannover_Germany_01.jpg/500px-Hannover_old_